<div style="border: 2px solid #1a5276; padding: 15px; text-align: center; margin-bottom: 20px;">
    <h1 style="color: #1a5276; margin: 0; font-size: 2em;">Lesson Planner – Theme # Saving for Future Goals! – Lesson # 3</h1>
    <p style="color: #1a5276; margin: 5px 0 0 0; font-size: 1.1em;">Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</p>
</div>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Lesson #:</b> 3</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Skills Focus:</b> Speaking</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Grade:</b> 12th Grade (CEFR: B1.3)</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Scenario:</b> My Personal Success Story</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Theme:</b> Saving for Future Goals!</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="2"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Specific Objective:</b> Speaking: Productive: Narrate a personal experience with learning a skill. Interactive: Engage in role-plays about navigating new environments.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Learning Outcome:</b> Speaking: Can narrate a personal experience of learning a valuable skill (e.g., "Learning to manage my finances has helped me save for my higher education.")<br>Can answer questions about skill development experiences (e.g., "What was the most challenging part of managing finances?" "The most challenging part of learning to manage my finances was creating a budget that I could stick to.")<br>Can write a reflective essay on a personal experience with saving or managing money, connecting it to future goals or aspirations (e.g., "Learning to budget my allowance has taught me discipline and patience. If I keep saving consistently, I will be able to afford paying my university tuition next year, which will help me become more independent.")</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276; text-align: center; margin-20px 0;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>
<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <thead>
        <tr>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f2f2f2; color: #1a5276;">Stage & Description</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f2f2f2; color: #1a5276;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f2f2f2; color: #1a5276;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</b><br><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Engagement, Modeling and Clarification)</p></td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Warm-up:</b> "Quick Chat: Future Aspirations." Students work in pairs to discuss a prompt displayed on the board: "What is one 'future-oriented' goal you have, and how have your 'savings' or 'finances' contributed to it so far? What 'initiative' have you taken?" They will share one idea with the class. This activates prior knowledge from Lessons 1 & 2.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Modeling:</b> The teacher models responses using target grammar and pronunciation. For example: "I have saved some money for a language course next summer. If I continue to be careful with my budget, I will be attending classes in July. It's an important investment in my career." The teacher explicitly demonstrates stressing content words ("SAVED," "MONEY," "LANGUAGE COURSE," "SUMMER," "CAREFUL," "BUDGET," "ATTENDING," "CLASSES," "JULY," "IMPORTANT," "INVESTMENT," "CAREER") and reducing stress on auxiliary verbs ("have," "will").</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Clarification (CCQs):</b> The teacher checks understanding of key terms and concepts.
                    <ul>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What does 'future-oriented' mean in the context of goals? Can you give an example?" (Expected: Related to future plans/aspirations, like "college" or "career growth.")</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"When I say 'initiative,' what kind of action am I referring to?" (Expected: Taking the first step, proactive effort, e.g., "starting a saving plan.")</li>
                    </ul>
                </p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">5-7 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">STAGE 2 — Presentation</b><br><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Input of new language/content connected to Scenario: "My Personal Success Story")</p></td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Material:</b> An audio recording (2-3 minutes) of a Panamanian young adult (or a simulated interview) sharing their personal experience of learning a skill, managing finances, or volunteering for 'community service' to achieve a 'long-term' goal. The recording will naturally integrate the target vocabulary (e.g., 'achievements,' 'goals,' 'finances,' 'investment,' 'strategies,' 'impact') and grammar (Present Perfect for past experiences, Future Continuous for future plans, First Conditional for discussing success).</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Communicative Competence:</b> Engaging in conversations on goals and aspirations, and respectfully discussing personal achievements.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Comprehension tasks:</b> Students listen to the audio twice.</p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Gist questions (after first listen):</b> "What 'skill' or 'achievement' is the person in the audio talking about? What is their main 'future goal'?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>True/False (after second listen):</b> Students answer T/F questions based on specific details (e.g., "The speaker has saved money by managing their allowance carefully." "If they continue their training, they will be leading a project next year."). Teacher reviews answers, clarifying any misunderstandings, especially around vocabulary and grammar in context.</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">8-10 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</b><br><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Accuracy focus on Speaking)</p></td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Oral practice of Present Perfect for achievements, Future Continuous for long-term goals, and First Conditional for discussing future success. Integration of vocabulary: 'success,' 'finances,' 'savings,' 'investment,' 'growth,' 'achievements,' 'opportunities,' 'strategies,' 'manage,' 'pursue,' 'aspire,' 'succeed.'</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Detailed Procedure:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>1. Controlled Practice: Sentence Builder Chain.</b> The teacher starts a sentence using target grammar and vocabulary (e.g., "I have saved money..."). Students, in a chain, complete the sentence orally, adding a related clause or phrase, then start a new one, focusing on correct grammar and stress. Example:
                        <br>Teacher: "I have SAVED some MONEY..."
                        <br>Student A: "...for my COLLEGE studies. If I continue, I will be PURSUING my DREAM career."
                        <br>Student B: "If I continue, I will be PURSUING my DREAM career, and I have ALREADY started some TRAINING."
                        <br>The teacher monitors for correct use of Present Perfect, Future Continuous, First Conditional, and pronunciation (stress on content words).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>2. Semi-controlled Practice: Goal Statement Prompts.</b> Students work in pairs. The teacher displays prompts related to personal success and future goals (e.g., "Talk about an 'essential' skill you have learned," "Describe what you will be 'managing' in five years," "Discuss an 'opportunity' you have had and what will happen 'if' you seize it."). Students take turns forming complete sentences orally using the target grammar and vocabulary. E.g., "I have learned an 'essential' skill: time management. If I use it wisely, I will be 'managing' my study projects effectively."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>3. Pair Interaction: "Achievement Q&A."</b> Students remain in pairs. They are given a list of question starters using the target grammar and vocabulary. They must ask their partner these questions and provide answers, actively listening and responding. E.g., "How has volunteering helped you grow?" (Pragmatic: respectfully discussing achievements) "What skills would you like to develop for your future goals?" (Pragmatic: engaging in conversations on goals and aspirations) "What significant 'achievements' have you had this year related to your 'personal growth'?" "What 'strategies' have you used to 'manage' your 'finances' for a 'long-term' goal?" "If you 'invest' your time in 'training,' what 'opportunities' will you be 'pursuing'?"</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">15-18 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</b><br><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Communicative task where students USE the language in a realistic scenario: "My Personal Success Story")</p></td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Task Format:</b> Role-Play: "The Future Goals Interview." Students work in groups of three. One student acts as an "Interviewer" (e.g., from a university admissions panel or a career mentor), and the other two are "Candidates" applying for an imaginary scholarship or professional development program related to their 'future goals' and 'career' aspirations. This directly aligns with the scenario "My Personal Success Story" and theme "Saving for Future Goals!".</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Procedure:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">The Interviewer asks questions about the Candidate's past 'achievements' (Present Perfect), their 'long-term' goals (Future Continuous), and what they plan to do to ensure 'success' (First Conditional).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Candidates must narrate a personal experience learning a valuable skill or managing their finances for a goal. They should integrate as many target vocabulary words as naturally possible (e.g., 'finances,' 'savings,' 'investment,' 'growth,' 'initiative,' 'opportunities,' 'strategies,' 'manage,' 'contribute,' 'succeed').</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Encourage natural pronunciation, stressing content words and reducing stress on auxiliaries for fluent communication.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">The teacher circulates, observing interaction, language use, and providing discreet support as needed.</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">10-12 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</b><br><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Formative assessment strategy)</p></td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Assessment Task:</b> Teacher observation of the "Future Goals Interview" role-play using a simple checklist focusing on the Speaking learning outcome. Peers can also provide brief feedback.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Evaluation Criteria:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Intelligible pronunciation (stressing content words).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Appropriate use of Present Perfect (achievements).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Appropriate use of Future Continuous (long-term goals).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Appropriate use of First Conditional (future success).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Integration of target vocabulary (e.g., 'finances,' 'savings,' 'investment,' 'growth,' 'opportunities,' 'manage,' 'aspire').</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Clarity of personal narrative or advice.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Collaborative interaction and respectful engagement (Sociolinguistic).</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b> Students complete two sentences on a slip of paper before leaving:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Today, I confidently used (Present Perfect / Future Continuous / First Conditional) to talk about my future plans."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"One 'strategy' I learned or shared today for 'managing' finances/goals was..."</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">5 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">STAGE 6 — Reflection</b></td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Student self-reflection prompt:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What part of today's speaking activities helped you articulate your personal success stories or future goals most effectively? What was the most 'challenging' aspect?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"How can you apply the skills of respectfully discussing 'achievements' and engaging in conversations about 'aspirations' outside the classroom?"</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Teacher reflection:</b> Most students were able to narrate their personal experiences using Present Perfect for achievements. The challenge was consistently integrating all three target grammar points (Present Perfect, Future Continuous, First Conditional) and a wide range of vocabulary naturally within the conversation. The pronunciation focus on stressing content words showed some improvement, but further emphasis will be beneficial. Some students needed more scaffolding to 'initiate' discussions and ensure all voices were heard in group activities (Sociolinguistic competence). For the next lesson, I will provide sentence starters that directly prompt the use of all three tenses and review the pronunciation points as a quick warm-up.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Connection to next lesson:</b> Today, we extensively practiced speaking about our 'personal success stories' and 'saving for future goals.' In our next lesson (Lesson 4: Writing Composition), we will transition these oral narratives and discussions into a written format. Students will write a reflective essay on a personal experience with saving or managing money, connecting it to future goals or aspirations, utilizing the grammar and vocabulary we practiced orally today.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">2-3 min</td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>